      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:9b50132a0261c653854bf960841444e3085bf795ee14eab29c07196fb59a42c6",
      "text": "LRRK2 (leucine-rich repeat kinase 2) is a Parkinson's disease target pursued with a small molecule inhibitor, BIIB122 (DNL151), and an intrathecal antisense oligonucleotide, BIIB094 (ION859). Biogen and Denali report that the Phase 2b LUMA study of BIIB122 in early-stage Parkinson\u2019s disease did not meet its primary or secondary endpoints, and that they will discontinue development in idiopathic Parkinson\u2019s disease while Denali continues the Phase 2a BEACON study in carriers of a pathogenic LRRK2 variant. The REASON phase 1 authors report cerebrospinal fluid LRRK2 and phosphorylated Rab10 lowered by up to 59% and up to 50% with BIIB094.",
      "sources": [
        "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03976349",
